      "message": "This covers HTTP/2, but on HTTP/1.1 RestconfSession.blockedRequests() holds every pipelined request without a bound, so an authenticated client can now park 1 MiB per request instead of 16 KiB. Is it worth stating that here, and tracking a follow-up to stop auto-read or cap the queue while a request is in flight?",
